  "preamble": "Monophthongization of diphthong [ai] to near-open front unrounded vowel [æ] through glide absorption and vowel quality change. As a regular historical change it is best documented in Slavic, where Balto-Slavic *ai became yat (*ě, generally reconstructed as [æː]) in Proto-Slavic, e.g. *snáigas > *sněgъ 'snow'.",
